Feature: What `generate` writes, and what it leaves alone
`generate` rewrites what kac derives from frontmatter and the schema, and `--check` reports what a run would rewrite.
docs/use/cli/generate.md and docs/reference/generation.md state each behaviour below. Driven against the generate,
generate-stale, generate-adoption and clean fixtures, through `Commands.Generate`.

Scenario: A run rewrites a stale index whole, and no other file
  Given the generate fixture corpus
  And "adrs/_index.md" ends with "A line nothing generated."
  When I generate
  Then it succeeds
  And only "adrs/_index.md" changed
  And "adrs/_index.md" does not contain "A line nothing generated."
  And the generated files are fresh

Scenario Outline: A run rewrites a block between its markers and keeps the words around it
  Given the generate fixture corpus
  And the generated blocks in "<page>" are emptied
  And "<page>" ends with "Words the corpus wrote."
  When I generate
  Then it succeeds
  And only "<page>" changed
  And "<page>" contains "Words the corpus wrote."
  And the generated files are fresh

Examples:
  | page                          |
  | adrs.md                       |
  | knowledge-as-code/taxonomy.md |

Scenario: A run over a fresh corpus writes nothing
  Given the generate fixture corpus
  When I generate
  Then it succeeds
  And nothing is written

Scenario: A second run over a corpus the first run rewrote writes nothing
  Given the clean fixture corpus
  And a first run has rewritten it
  When I generate
  Then it succeeds
  And nothing is written

Scenario: A check over a fresh corpus passes
  Given the generate fixture corpus
  When I check the generated files
  Then it succeeds

Scenario: A check over a stale corpus fails and writes nothing
  Given the generate-stale fixture corpus
  When I check the generated files
  Then it fails
  And nothing is written

Scenario: A type the descriptor does not adopt gets no index
  Given the generate-adoption fixture corpus
  When I generate
  Then it succeeds
  And nothing is written
  And "policies/_index.md" does not exist

Scenario: A type adopted with no folder is not created
  Given the generate-adoption fixture corpus
  And the descriptor adopts "glossary" as well
  When I generate
  Then it succeeds
  And nothing is written
  And "glossary" does not exist

Scenario: An index takes its columns and its order from the schema, under a banner
  Given the clean fixture corpus
  When I generate
  Then it succeeds
  And "deviations/_index.md" begins with "<!-- Generated by kac tooling - do not edit by hand -->"
  And the tables in "deviations/_index.md" are headed:
    | columns                                                 |
    | ID, Title, Status, Risk, Departs from, Review by, Owner |
  And "deviations/_index.md" does not contain "## "
  And "deviations/_index.md" lists, in order:
    | text               |
    | dev-technical-debt |
    | dev-clean-baseline |

Scenario: An index heads a table for each folder below the type
  Given the clean fixture corpus
  When I generate
  Then it succeeds
  And "standards/_index.md" lists, in order:
    | text        |
    | ## Common   |
    | std-TEST    |
    | ## Platform |
    | std-NODE    |
  And the tables in "standards/_index.md" are headed:
    | columns                                              |
    | ID, Title, Status, Derived from, Review by           |
    | ID, Title, Category, Status, Derived from, Review by |

Scenario: A type with no records gets an index saying so
  Given the clean fixture corpus
  And "adrs/0001-clean-baseline.md" is deleted
  When I generate
  Then it succeeds
  And "adrs/_index.md" contains "_Nothing here yet."
  And "adrs/_index.md" does not contain "|"

Scenario: A type page lists the universal fields it refines, and only the checks its type can trip
  Given the generate fixture corpus
  And the generated blocks in "adrs.md" are emptied
  When I generate
  Then it succeeds
  And "adrs.md" lists, in order:
    | text                              |
    | `tier` *†                         |
    | `status` *†                       |
    | `decided-on`                      |
    | The day the decision was settled. |
    | `related`                         |
    | universal checks                  |
    | `y-statement`                     |
  And "adrs.md" does not contain "`id` *†"
  And "adrs.md" does not contain "`tags` †"
  And "adrs.md" does not contain "`frontmatter-parses`"
  And "adrs.md" does not contain "`derived-key`"
  And "adrs.md" does not contain "`part-id-unique / part-ref`"
  And "adrs.md" does not contain "`draft-expiry`"

Scenario: The metadata page lists the universal checks once
  Given the generate fixture corpus
  And the generated blocks in "knowledge-as-code/metadata.md" are emptied
  When I generate
  Then it succeeds
  And only "knowledge-as-code/metadata.md" changed
  And "knowledge-as-code/metadata.md" lists, in order:
    | text                 |
    | `frontmatter-parses` |
    | `unused-definition`  |
  And "knowledge-as-code/metadata.md" does not contain "`y-statement`"

Scenario: A block whose markers are gone is left unwritten, and validate reports it
  Given the generate fixture corpus
  And the "schema-adrs" block in "adrs.md" is deleted
  When I generate
  And I validate the corpus
  Then it succeeds
  And nothing is written
  And the findings for "adrs.md" are exactly:
    | line | check           | message                                                                                                                    |
    |      | generated-block | the 'schema-adrs' block is missing its markers: `kac generate` writes between them and leaves the page alone without both. |

Scenario: A corpus declines the README block by deleting its markers
  Given the generate fixture corpus
  And the "types-index" block in "README.md" is deleted
  When I generate
  And I validate the corpus
  Then it succeeds
  And nothing is written
  And the findings for "README.md" are exactly:
    | line | check | message |

Scenario: The types graph keeps to the Mermaid subset
  Given the generate fixture corpus
  And the generated blocks in "knowledge-as-code/taxonomy.md" are emptied
  When I generate
  Then it succeeds
  And the types graph in "knowledge-as-code/taxonomy.md" keeps to the Mermaid subset
